/-!
# Alternating-group polynomial invariants and nonfinite SAGBI bases

This file studies the polynomial invariant subalgebra
`MvPolynomial.permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R` of the alternating group
`A_n ≤ S_n`.

Let `Δ_n = ∏_{i < j} (X_i - X_j)` be the Vandermonde difference product
(`MvPolynomial.vandermondeDiff n R`). Reindexing `Matrix.det_vandermonde` along the order-reversing
permutation `Fin.revPerm` identifies `Δ_n` with the staircase alternant
`TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (fun j => n - 1 - j)`. From this identification follow:

* `Δ_n` is antisymmetric (`rename σ Δ_n = sign σ • Δ_n`), hence `A_n`-invariant, and `Δ_n ^ 2` is
  symmetric, defining the universal discriminant polynomial `MvPolynomial.discriminantPoly n R` in
  the elementary symmetric coordinates `e₁, …, eₙ`.
* In lexicographic order `X 0 > X 1 > … > X (n - 1)`, `Δ_n` is monic with leading exponent
  `j ↦ n - 1 - j`; consequently `Δ_n` is a non-zero-divisor (`IsRegular`) in
  `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` over every commutative ring `R`.
* Over any commutative ring `R` in which `2` is a unit, every antisymmetric polynomial factors as a
  symmetric polynomial times `Δ_n` (via Jacobi's bialternant formula
  `TauCeti.diagramSchurPoly_mul_alternant`), and for `2 ≤ n` the alternating invariant algebra has
  the presentation
  `R[e₁, …, eₙ, Δ] / (Δ² - Dₙ) ≃ₐ[R] permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R`.

For SAGBI bases:

* When `n = 1`, `A₁ = ⊥`, the invariant algebra is the whole ring `R[X 0]`, and `{X 0}` is a
  singleton `m`-SAGBI basis for every monomial order `m`.
* When `n ≥ 3`, `A_n` is not generated by transpositions, so the permutation SAGBI criterion
  (`MonomialOrder.exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff`) immediately shows that
  `permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R` admits no finite `m`-SAGBI basis for any
  monomial order `m` over any nontrivial commutative semiring without zero divisors (in particular
  over any field in any characteristic).
* In three variables under lexicographic order `x > y > z` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, the explicit
  invariant `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2 = x² z + x y² + y z² + (3 / 2) x y z` has leading monomial `x² z`,
  whose exponent `(2, 0, 1)` lies outside the additive submonoid generated by the leading exponents
  `x`, `x y`, `x y z`, `x² y` of the algebra generators `e₁, e₂, e₃, Δ₃`.

## Main definitions

* `MvPolynomial.vandermondeDiff n R`: the Vandermonde difference product
  `∏_{i < j} (X i - X j)`.
* `MvPolynomial.discriminantPoly n R`: the unique polynomial `D_n` in the elementary symmetric
  coordinates satisfying `aeval (e₁, …, eₙ) D_n = Δ_n ^ 2`.
* `MvPolynomial.alternatingPresentationHom n R`: the `R`-algebra homomorphism
  `MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R →ₐ[R] permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R`
  sending `some i ↦ e_{i + 1}` and `none ↦ Δ_n`.
* `MvPolynomial.alternatingPresentationEquiv`: for `2 ≤ n` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, the quotient
  algebra isomorphism
  `(MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R ⧸ Ideal.span {X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)})
    ≃ₐ[R] permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R`.
* `MvPolynomial.alternatingThreeWitness`: the explicit three-variable `A₃`-invariant
  `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2`.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant`: `Δ_n` equals the staircase alternant.
* `MvPolynomial.isRegular_vandermondeDiff`: `Δ_n` is regular over any commutative ring `R`.
* `MvPolynomial.exists_eq_mul_vandermondeDiff_of_antisymm`: over any commutative ring with
  `IsUnit (2 : R)`, every antisymmetric polynomial is a symmetric polynomial times `Δ_n`.
* `MvPolynomial.ker_alternatingPresentationHom`: for `2 ≤ n` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, the kernel of
  `alternatingPresentationHom n R` is the principal ideal `(X none ^ 2 - rename some D_n)`.
* `MonomialOrder.isSAGBIBasis_singleton_X_zero_alternatingGroup_one`: `{X 0}` is a singleton
  `m`-SAGBI basis for `A₁` for every monomial order `m`.
* `MonomialOrder.not_exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_alternatingGroup`: for `3 ≤ n`, every monomial
  order `m`, and every nontrivial commutative semiring `R` without zero divisors, the
  `A_n`-invariant subalgebra has no finite `m`-SAGBI basis.
* `MonomialOrder.lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness` and
  `MonomialOrder.lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness_notMem_closure`: the leading monomial of
  `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` in lex `x > y > z` is `x² z`, outside `⟨x, x y, x y z, x² y⟩`.

## References

* L. Robbiano, M. Sweedler, *Subalgebra bases*, in *Commutative Algebra (Salvador, 1988)*,
  Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1430, Springer, 1990, 61–87.
* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 11.
* M. Göbel, *A constructive description of SAGBI bases for polynomial invariants of permutation
  groups*, J. Symbolic Comput. **26** (1998).
* N. M. Thiéry, S. Thomassé, *Convex cones and SAGBI bases of permutation invariants*, in
  *Invariant Theory in All Characteristics*, CRM Proc. Lecture Notes 35, AMS, 2004.
-/

public section

open Equiv

/-! ### The Vandermonde difference product and antisymmetric factorization -/

namespace MvPolynomial

variable {n : ℕ} {R : Type*}

/-- The Vandermonde difference product `Δ_n = ∏_{i < j} (X_i - X_j)` in `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R`. -/
noncomputable def vandermondeDiff (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R :=
  ∏ i : Fin n, ∏ j ∈ Finset.Ioi i, (X i - X j)

/-- The Vandermonde difference product equals the staircase alternant
`det (X_i ^ (n - 1 - j))`. -/
theorem vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    vandermondeDiff n R = TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (fun j => n - 1 - (j : ℕ)) := by
  let A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) :=
    Matrix.vandermonde (X : Fin n → MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)
  have hcol : (A.submatrix id Fin.revPerm).det =
      TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (fun j => n - 1 - (j : ℕ)) := by
    rw [TauCeti.alternant_def]
    congr 1
    refine Matrix.ext fun i j => ?_
    simp only [Matrix.submatrix_apply, id_eq, A, Matrix.vandermonde_apply, Fin.revPerm_apply,
      Fin.val_rev, Matrix.of_apply]
    congr 1
    omega
  have hrow : (A.submatrix Fin.revPerm id).det =
      ∏ i : Fin n, ∏ j ∈ Finset.Ioi i, (X (Fin.revPerm j) - X (Fin.revPerm i)) := by
    have hmat : A.submatrix Fin.revPerm id =
        Matrix.vandermonde (fun i : Fin n => (X (Fin.revPerm i) : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) := by
      ext i j
      simp [A, Matrix.vandermonde]
    rw [hmat, Matrix.det_vandermonde]
  have hdet_eq : (A.submatrix id Fin.revPerm).det = (A.submatrix Fin.revPerm id).det := by
    rw [Matrix.det_permute' Fin.revPerm A, Matrix.det_permute Fin.revPerm A]
  rw [← hcol, hdet_eq, hrow, vandermondeDiff]
  let S : Finset (Fin n × Fin n) := Finset.univ.filter fun p => p.1 < p.2
  have hprod_eq : ∀ f : Fin n → Fin n → MvPolynomial (Fin n) R,
      (∏ i : Fin n, ∏ j ∈ Finset.Ioi i, f i j) = ∏ p ∈ S, f p.1 p.2 := fun f => by
    rw [Finset.prod_sigma']
    refine Finset.prod_bij (fun p _ => (p.1, p.2))
      (fun p hp => by
        simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and]
        exact Finset.mem_Ioi.mp (Finset.mem_sigma.mp hp).2)
      (fun p₁ _ p₂ _ h => by
        cases p₁; cases p₂; cases h; rfl)
      (fun p hp => ⟨⟨p.1, p.2⟩,
        Finset.mem_sigma.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _,
          Finset.mem_Ioi.mpr (Finset.mem_filter.mp hp).2⟩, rfl⟩)
      (fun _ _ => rfl)
  rw [hprod_eq, hprod_eq]
  refine Finset.prod_bij (fun p _ => (Fin.revPerm p.2, Fin.revPerm p.1))
    (fun p hp => by
      simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hp ⊢
      exact Fin.rev_lt_rev.mpr hp)
    (fun p₁ _ p₂ _ h => by
      have h1 := Fin.revPerm.injective (congrArg Prod.fst h)
      have h2 := Fin.revPerm.injective (congrArg Prod.snd h)
      exact Prod.ext h2 h1)
    (fun p hp => ⟨(Fin.revPerm p.2, Fin.revPerm p.1), by
      simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hp ⊢
      exact Fin.rev_lt_rev.mpr hp, by simp⟩)
    (fun _ _ => by simp)

/-- Permuting the variables of `vandermondeDiff n R` multiplies it by the sign of the
permutation. -/
@[simp]
theorem rename_vandermondeDiff [CommRing R] (σ : Perm (Fin n)) :
    rename σ (vandermondeDiff n R) = Perm.sign σ • vandermondeDiff n R := by
  rw [vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant, TauCeti.rename_alternant]

/-- `vandermondeDiff n R` is invariant under the alternating group `alternatingGroup (Fin n)`. -/
theorem vandermondeDiff_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra_alternatingGroup (n : ℕ) (R : Type*)
    [CommRing R] :
    vandermondeDiff n R ∈ permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R := by
  rw [mem_permInvariantSubalgebra]
  intro σ hσ
  rw [rename_vandermondeDiff, Perm.mem_alternatingGroup.mp hσ, one_smul]

/-- The square of `vandermondeDiff n R` is a symmetric polynomial. -/
theorem vandermondeDiff_sq_mem_symmetricSubalgebra (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    vandermondeDiff n R ^ 2 ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R := by
  rw [mem_symmetricSubalgebra]
  intro σ
  rw [map_pow, rename_vandermondeDiff, Units.smul_def, zsmul_eq_mul, mul_pow,
    ← Int.cast_pow, ← Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, Int.units_sq]
  simp

/-- In lexicographic order `X 0 > X 1 > … > X (n - 1)`, the degree of `vandermondeDiff n R` is the
staircase exponent `j ↦ n - 1 - j`. -/
theorem lex_degree_vandermondeDiff (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] :
    MonomialOrder.lex.degree (vandermondeDiff n R) =
      Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm (fun j : Fin n => n - 1 - (j : ℕ)) := by
  let δ : Fin n →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm (fun j : Fin n => n - 1 - (j : ℕ))
  have hcoeff_δ : (vandermondeDiff n R).coeff δ = 1 := by
    rw [vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant]
    have h := TauCeti.coeff_alternant_of_injective (R := R) (TauCeti.injective_staircase n) 1
    simpa [δ] using h
  apply MonomialOrder.lex.toSyn.injective
  refine le_antisymm (MonomialOrder.lex.degree_le_iff.2 fun d hd => ?_) ?_
  · rw [mem_support_iff, vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant, TauCeti.coeff_alternant (R := R)] at hd
    have hne : (Finset.univ.filter fun τ : Perm (Fin n) =>
        ⇑d ∘ ⇑τ = fun j : Fin n => n - 1 - (j : ℕ)).Nonempty := by
      by_contra hemp
      rw [Finset.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at hemp
      exact hd (by simp [hemp])
    obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ := hne
    have hτeq : ⇑d ∘ ⇑τ = fun j : Fin n => n - 1 - (j : ℕ) := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hτ).2
    have hd_val : ∀ i : Fin n, d i = n - 1 - (τ.symm i : ℕ) := fun i => by
      have := congrFun hτeq (τ.symm i)
      simpa using this
    rcases eq_or_ne d δ with rfl | hne_d
    · exact le_rfl
    · apply le_of_lt
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
      have hex : ∃ i : Fin n, d i ≠ δ i := by
        by_contra hall
        push Not at hall
        exact hne_d (Finsupp.ext hall)
      let Sdiff : Finset (Fin n) := Finset.univ.filter fun j => d j ≠ δ j
      have hSdiff : Sdiff.Nonempty := by
        obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hex
        exact ⟨j, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hj⟩⟩
      let i₀ : Fin n := Sdiff.min' hSdiff
      have hi₀_ne : d i₀ ≠ δ i₀ := (Finset.mem_filter.mp (Finset.min'_mem Sdiff hSdiff)).2
      have hlt_eq : ∀ j : Fin n, j < i₀ → d j = δ j := fun j hj => by
        by_contra hne_j
        exact not_le_of_gt hj
          (Finset.min'_le Sdiff j (Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hne_j⟩))
      have hfix : ∀ j : Fin n, j < i₀ → τ.symm j = j := fun j hj => by
        have h := hlt_eq j hj
        rw [hd_val j] at h
        have hδj : δ j = n - 1 - (j : ℕ) := by simp [δ]
        rw [hδj] at h
        exact TauCeti.injective_staircase n h
      have hτ_ne : τ.symm i₀ ≠ i₀ := fun heq => hi₀_ne (by
        rw [hd_val i₀, heq]; simp [δ])
      have hτ_gt : i₀ < τ.symm i₀ := by
        rcases lt_trichotomy (τ.symm i₀) i₀ with hlt | heq | hgt
        · exact absurd (τ.symm.injective (hfix (τ.symm i₀) hlt)) hτ_ne
        · exact absurd heq hτ_ne
        · exact hgt
      refine ⟨i₀, fun j hj => hlt_eq j hj, ?_⟩
      change d i₀ < δ i₀
      rw [hd_val i₀]
      have hδi : δ i₀ = n - 1 - (i₀ : ℕ) := by simp [δ]
      rw [hδi]
      have : (i₀ : ℕ) < (τ.symm i₀ : ℕ) := Fin.lt_def.mp hτ_gt
      have : (τ.symm i₀ : ℕ) < n := (τ.symm i₀).isLt
      omega
  · apply MonomialOrder.lex.le_degree
    rw [mem_support_iff, hcoeff_δ]
    exact one_ne_zero

/-- In lexicographic order, `vandermondeDiff n R` is monic (`leadingCoeff = 1`). -/
theorem lex_leadingCoeff_vandermondeDiff (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] :
    MonomialOrder.lex.leadingCoeff (vandermondeDiff n R) = 1 := by
  rw [MonomialOrder.leadingCoeff, lex_degree_vandermondeDiff, vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant]
  have h := TauCeti.coeff_alternant_of_injective (R := R) (TauCeti.injective_staircase n) 1
  simpa using h

/-- `vandermondeDiff n R` is a non-zero-divisor in `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` over every commutative
ring `R`. -/
theorem isRegular_vandermondeDiff (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    IsRegular (vandermondeDiff n R) := by
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with _ | _
  · exact ⟨fun _ _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _, fun _ _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  · have hreg_lc : IsRegular (MonomialOrder.lex.leadingCoeff (vandermondeDiff n R)) := by
      rw [lex_leadingCoeff_vandermondeDiff]
      exact isRegular_one
    have hright : IsRightRegular (vandermondeDiff n R) := fun a b hab => by
      dsimp only at hab
      have hsub : (a - b) * vandermondeDiff n R = 0 := by rw [sub_mul, hab, sub_self]
      have hlc : MonomialOrder.lex.leadingCoeff ((a - b) * vandermondeDiff n R) = 0 := by
        rw [hsub, MonomialOrder.leadingCoeff_zero]
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex.leadingCoeff_mul_of_isRegular_right hreg_lc,
        lex_leadingCoeff_vandermondeDiff, mul_one] at hlc
      exact sub_eq_zero.mp (MonomialOrder.lex.leadingCoeff_eq_zero_iff.mp hlc)
    exact ⟨fun a b hab => hright (by simpa [mul_comm] using hab), hright⟩

/-- Sorting an injective map `Fin n → ℕ` in strictly decreasing order by a unique permutation. -/
private theorem existsUnique_strictAnti_comp {f : Fin n → ℕ} (hf : Function.Injective f) :
    ∃! p : Perm (Fin n), StrictAnti (f ∘ p) := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hq_uniq⟩ := Equiv.Perm.existsUnique_strictMono_comp hf
  refine ⟨q * Fin.revPerm, fun a b hab => ?_, fun p hp => ?_⟩
  · change f (q (Fin.revPerm b)) < f (q (Fin.revPerm a))
    exact hq (Fin.rev_lt_rev.mpr hab)
  · have hmono : StrictMono (f ∘ ⇑(p * (Fin.revPerm : Perm (Fin n)))) := fun a b hab => by
      change f ((p * (Fin.revPerm : Perm (Fin n))) a) < f ((p * (Fin.revPerm : Perm (Fin n))) b)
      rw [Perm.mul_apply, Perm.mul_apply, Fin.revPerm_apply, Fin.revPerm_apply]
      exact hp (Fin.rev_lt_rev.mpr hab)
    have hpeq : p * Fin.revPerm = q := hq_uniq (p * Fin.revPerm) hmono
    calc p = (p * Fin.revPerm) * Fin.revPerm := by
            ext i; simp [Perm.mul_apply]
      _ = q * Fin.revPerm := by rw [hpeq]

/-- Over a commutative ring in which `2` is a unit, an antisymmetric polynomial has zero
coefficient at every exponent vector with a repeated entry. -/
private theorem coeff_eq_zero_of_not_injective_of_antisymm [CommRing R] (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R))
    {g : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R} (hg : ∀ σ : Perm (Fin n), rename σ g = Perm.sign σ • g)
    {d : Fin n →₀ ℕ} (hnot : ¬ Function.Injective (⇑d : Fin n → ℕ)) :
    g.coeff d = 0 := by
  simp only [Function.Injective, not_forall] at hnot
  obtain ⟨i, j, hij, hne⟩ := hnot
  let τ : Perm (Fin n) := swap i j
  have hd_fix : d.equivMapDomain τ = d := by
    ext k
    rw [Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply, Equiv.symm_swap]
    rcases eq_or_ne k i with rfl | hki
    · simp [hij]
    · rcases eq_or_ne k j with rfl | hkj
      · simp [hij]
      · simp [swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hki hkj]
  have hneg : g.coeff d = -g.coeff d := by
    have h1 := coeff_rename_equivMapDomain τ g d
    rw [hd_fix, hg τ, Perm.sign_swap hne] at h1
    simpa using h1.symm
  have h2mul : (2 : R) * g.coeff d = 0 := by
    rw [two_mul]
    calc g.coeff d + g.coeff d = g.coeff d + (-g.coeff d) := by nth_rw 2 [hneg]
      _ = 0 := add_neg_cancel _
  exact h2.mul_right_eq_zero.mp h2mul

/-- **Antisymmetric factorization theorem:** over any commutative ring `R` in which `2` is a unit,
every antisymmetric polynomial `g` in `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` factors as `h * vandermondeDiff n R`
for some symmetric polynomial `h ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R`. -/
theorem exists_eq_mul_vandermondeDiff_of_antisymm [CommRing R] (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R))
    {g : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R} (hg : ∀ σ : Perm (Fin n), rename σ g = Perm.sign σ • g) :
    ∃ h ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R, g = h * vandermondeDiff n R := by
  classical
  let S : Finset (Fin n →₀ ℕ) := g.support.filter fun d => StrictAnti (⇑d : Fin n → ℕ)
  have hg_eq : g = ∑ d ∈ S, C (g.coeff d) * TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (⇑d) := by
    ext e
    rw [coeff_sum]
    by_cases hinj : Function.Injective (⇑e : Fin n → ℕ)
    · obtain ⟨τ₀, hτ₀, hτ₀_uniq⟩ := existsUnique_strictAnti_comp hinj
      let d₀ : Fin n →₀ ℕ := e.equivMapDomain τ₀⁻¹
      have hd₀_fun : (⇑d₀ : Fin n → ℕ) = ⇑e ∘ ⇑τ₀ := by
        funext i
        simp [d₀, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply, Perm.inv_def]
      have hd₀_anti : StrictAnti (⇑d₀ : Fin n → ℕ) := hd₀_fun ▸ hτ₀
      have he_eq : e = Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm (⇑d₀ ∘ ⇑τ₀⁻¹) := by
        ext i
        simp [d₀, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply, Perm.inv_def]
      have hterm_zero : ∀ d ∈ S, d ≠ d₀ →
          (C (g.coeff d) * TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (⇑d)).coeff e = 0 := fun d hd hne => by
        rw [coeff_C_mul, TauCeti.coeff_alternant]
        suffices (Finset.univ.filter fun ρ : Perm (Fin n) => ⇑e ∘ ⇑ρ = ⇑d) = ∅ by
          simp [this]
        rw [Finset.filter_eq_empty_iff]
        intro ρ _ hρ
        have hρ_anti : StrictAnti (⇑e ∘ ⇑ρ) := hρ ▸ (Finset.mem_filter.mp hd).2
        have hρ_eq : ρ = τ₀ := hτ₀_uniq ρ hρ_anti
        exact hne (Finsupp.ext fun i => by rw [← hρ, hρ_eq, ← hd₀_fun])
      have hsign_coeff : g.coeff e = g.coeff d₀ * ((Perm.sign τ₀⁻¹ : ℤ) : R) := by
        have h1 := coeff_rename_equivMapDomain τ₀⁻¹ g e
        rw [hg τ₀⁻¹, Units.smul_def, zsmul_eq_mul, ← map_intCast (C : R →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) R),
          coeff_C_mul] at h1
        rw [← h1, mul_comm]
      by_cases hd₀_mem : d₀ ∈ S
      · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single d₀ (fun d hd hne => hterm_zero d hd hne)
          (fun hnot => absurd hd₀_mem hnot), coeff_C_mul, he_eq,
          TauCeti.coeff_alternant_of_injective hd₀_anti.injective τ₀⁻¹, ← he_eq, hsign_coeff]
      · have hg_d₀ : g.coeff d₀ = 0 := by
          by_contra hne0
          exact hd₀_mem (Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨mem_support_iff.mpr hne0, hd₀_anti⟩)
        rw [hsign_coeff, hg_d₀, zero_mul]
        symm
        refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun d hd => hterm_zero d hd (fun heq => hd₀_mem (heq ▸ hd))
    · rw [coeff_eq_zero_of_not_injective_of_antisymm h2 hg hinj]
      symm
      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun d hd => ?_
      rw [coeff_C_mul, TauCeti.coeff_alternant]
      have hemp : (Finset.univ.filter fun ρ : Perm (Fin n) => ⇑e ∘ ⇑ρ = ⇑d) = ∅ := by
        rw [Finset.filter_eq_empty_iff]
        intro ρ _ hρ
        have hd_inj : Function.Injective (⇑d : Fin n → ℕ) := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hd).2.injective
        exact hinj (fun a b hab => ρ.symm.injective (hd_inj (by
          have ha := congrFun hρ (ρ.symm a)
          have hb := congrFun hρ (ρ.symm b)
          simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at ha hb
          rw [← ha, ← hb, hab])))
      simp [hemp]
  have hfactor : ∀ d ∈ S, ∃ s ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R,
      TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (⇑d) = s * vandermondeDiff n R := fun d hd => by
    obtain ⟨μ, hμ, hβ⟩ :=
      YoungDiagram.exists_eq_betaNumber_of_strictAnti (Finset.mem_filter.mp hd).2
    refine ⟨TauCeti.diagramSchurPoly n R μ, TauCeti.isSymmetric_diagramSchurPoly n R μ, ?_⟩
    rw [vandermondeDiff_eq_alternant, TauCeti.diagramSchurPoly_mul_alternant n μ hμ]
    congr 1
    exact funext fun j => (hβ j).symm
  choose s hs hseq using hfactor
  refine ⟨∑ d ∈ S.attach, C (g.coeff d.1) * s d.1 d.2,
    Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun d _ =>
      Subalgebra.mul_mem _ (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _) (hs d.1 d.2),
    ?_⟩
  calc g = ∑ d ∈ S, C (g.coeff d) * TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (⇑d) := hg_eq
    _ = ∑ d ∈ S.attach, C (g.coeff d.1) * TauCeti.alternant (Fin n) R (⇑d.1) :=
        (Finset.sum_attach S _).symm
    _ = ∑ d ∈ S.attach, (C (g.coeff d.1) * s d.1 d.2) * vandermondeDiff n R :=
        Finset.sum_congr rfl fun d _ => by rw [hseq d.1 d.2, mul_assoc]
    _ = (∑ d ∈ S.attach, C (g.coeff d.1) * s d.1 d.2) * vandermondeDiff n R :=
        (Finset.sum_mul _ _ _).symm

/-! ### Presentation of the alternating invariant algebra (`2 ≤ n`, `IsUnit (2 : R)`) -/

/-- The universal discriminant polynomial `D_n` in the elementary symmetric coordinates `e₁, …, eₙ`:
the unique polynomial satisfying `aeval (fun i => esymm (Fin n) R (i + 1)) D_n = Δ_n ^ 2`. -/
noncomputable def discriminantPoly (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R :=
  (esymmAlgEquiv (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n)).symm
    ⟨vandermondeDiff n R ^ 2, vandermondeDiff_sq_mem_symmetricSubalgebra n R⟩

/-- Evaluating `discriminantPoly n R` at the elementary symmetric polynomials `e₁, …, eₙ` recovers
`vandermondeDiff n R ^ 2`. -/
theorem aeval_esymm_discriminantPoly (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) (discriminantPoly n R) =
      vandermondeDiff n R ^ 2 := by
  rw [← esymmAlgHom_apply, ← esymmAlgEquiv_apply (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n),
    discriminantPoly, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- The `R`-algebra homomorphism from `MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R` to
`permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R` sending `X (some i)` to `e_{i + 1}` and
`X none` to `vandermondeDiff n R`. -/
noncomputable def alternatingPresentationHom (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R →ₐ[R]
      permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R :=
  aeval (Option.elim'
    ⟨vandermondeDiff n R, vandermondeDiff_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra_alternatingGroup n R⟩
    fun i : Fin n =>
      ⟨esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1),
        symmetricSubalgebra_le_permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n))
          (esymm_isSymmetric (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1))⟩)

@[simp]
theorem alternatingPresentationHom_X_none (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    ((alternatingPresentationHom n R (X none) :
        permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R) : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) =
      vandermondeDiff n R := by
  simp [alternatingPresentationHom]

@[simp]
theorem alternatingPresentationHom_X_some (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (i : Fin n) :
    ((alternatingPresentationHom n R (X (some i)) :
        permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R) : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) =
      esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1) := by
  simp [alternatingPresentationHom]

@[simp]
theorem alternatingPresentationHom_rename_some (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) :
    ((alternatingPresentationHom n R (rename some p) :
        permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R) : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) =
      aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) p := by
  have hcomp :
      ((permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R).val.comp
          (alternatingPresentationHom n R)).comp (rename some) =
        aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) := by
    apply MvPolynomial.algHom_ext
    intro i
    simp [alternatingPresentationHom]
  exact AlgHom.congr_fun hcomp p

/-- The discriminant-square relation `X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)` lies in the
kernel of `alternatingPresentationHom n R`. -/
theorem alternatingPresentationHom_discriminant_rel (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    alternatingPresentationHom n R
      (X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)) = 0 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  simp [aeval_esymm_discriminantPoly]

/-- Every `A_n`-invariant polynomial (`2 ≤ n`, `IsUnit (2 : R)`) decomposes uniquely as
`s + h * vandermondeDiff n R` with `s, h ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R`. -/
theorem existsUnique_symmetric_add_mul_vandermondeDiff {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) {p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R}
    (hp : p ∈ permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R) :
    ∃! sh : symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R × symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R,
      p = (sh.1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) +
        (sh.2 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) * vandermondeDiff n R := by
  let i0 : Fin n := ⟨0, by omega⟩
  let i1 : Fin n := ⟨1, by omega⟩
  have h01 : i0 ≠ i1 := by simp [i0, i1, Fin.ext_iff]
  let τ₀ : Perm (Fin n) := swap i0 i1
  have hsign_τ₀ : Perm.sign τ₀ = -1 := Perm.sign_swap h01
  have hrename_even : ∀ σ : Perm (Fin n), Perm.sign σ = 1 →
      rename σ p = p ∧ rename σ (rename τ₀ p) = rename τ₀ p := fun σ hσ => by
    have h1 : rename σ p = p :=
      mem_permInvariantSubalgebra.mp hp σ (Perm.mem_alternatingGroup.mpr hσ)
    have hconj : τ₀ * σ * τ₀ ∈ alternatingGroup (Fin n) := by
      rw [Perm.mem_alternatingGroup, map_mul, map_mul, hσ, hsign_τ₀]
      simp
    have h2' : rename σ (rename τ₀ p) = rename τ₀ p := by
      rw [rename_rename]
      have hcomp : (⇑σ ∘ ⇑τ₀ : Fin n → Fin n) = ⇑τ₀ ∘ ⇑(τ₀ * σ * τ₀) := funext fun x => by
        change σ (τ₀ x) = τ₀ ((τ₀ * σ * τ₀) x)
        simp [Perm.mul_apply, τ₀]
      rw [hcomp, ← rename_rename, mem_permInvariantSubalgebra.mp hp _ hconj]
    exact ⟨h1, h2'⟩
  have hrename_odd : ∀ σ : Perm (Fin n), Perm.sign σ = -1 →
      rename σ p = rename τ₀ p ∧ rename σ (rename τ₀ p) = p := fun σ hσ => by
    have hmul1 : τ₀ * σ ∈ alternatingGroup (Fin n) := by
      rw [Perm.mem_alternatingGroup, map_mul, hsign_τ₀, hσ]; simp
    have hmul2 : σ * τ₀ ∈ alternatingGroup (Fin n) := by
      rw [Perm.mem_alternatingGroup, map_mul, hσ, hsign_τ₀]; simp
    have h1 : rename σ p = rename τ₀ p := by
      have hcomp : (⇑σ : Fin n → Fin n) = ⇑τ₀ ∘ ⇑(τ₀ * σ) := funext fun x => by
        change σ x = τ₀ ((τ₀ * σ) x)
        simp [Perm.mul_apply, τ₀]
      rw [hcomp, ← rename_rename, mem_permInvariantSubalgebra.mp hp _ hmul1]
    have h2' : rename σ (rename τ₀ p) = p := by
      rw [rename_rename]
      exact mem_permInvariantSubalgebra.mp hp (σ * τ₀) hmul2
    exact ⟨h1, h2'⟩
  let uinv : R := (h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ)
  have huinv : (2 : R) * uinv = 1 := by
    change (h2.unit : R) * (h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) = 1
    exact_mod_cast Units.mul_inv h2.unit
  let s : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := C uinv * (p + rename τ₀ p)
  let g : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := C uinv * (p - rename τ₀ p)
  have hs_symm : s ∈ symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R := by
    rw [mem_symmetricSubalgebra]
    intro σ
    rw [map_mul, rename_C, map_add]
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or (Perm.sign σ) with hσ | hσ
    · rw [(hrename_even σ hσ).1, (hrename_even σ hσ).2]
    · rw [(hrename_odd σ hσ).1, (hrename_odd σ hσ).2, add_comm]
  have hg_anti : ∀ σ : Perm (Fin n), rename σ g = Perm.sign σ • g := fun σ => by
    rw [map_mul, rename_C, map_sub]
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or (Perm.sign σ) with hσ | hσ
    · rw [hσ, one_smul, (hrename_even σ hσ).1, (hrename_even σ hσ).2]
    · rw [hσ, Units.smul_def, Units.val_neg, Units.val_one, neg_one_zsmul,
        (hrename_odd σ hσ).1, (hrename_odd σ hσ).2]
      ring
  obtain ⟨h, hh_symm, hgeq⟩ := exists_eq_mul_vandermondeDiff_of_antisymm h2 hg_anti
  have hp_eq : p = s + h * vandermondeDiff n R := by
    rw [← hgeq]
    have hsum : s + g = C ((2 : R) * uinv) * p := by
      simp only [s, g, map_mul, map_ofNat]
      ring
    rw [hsum, huinv, map_one, one_mul]
  refine ⟨(⟨s, hs_symm⟩, ⟨h, hh_symm⟩), hp_eq, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨⟨s', hs'⟩, ⟨h', hh'⟩⟩ heq
  have hdiff : (s' - s) + (h' - h) * vandermondeDiff n R = 0 := by
    have : (s' + h' * vandermondeDiff n R) - (s + h * vandermondeDiff n R) = 0 := by
      rw [← heq, ← hp_eq, sub_self]
    linear_combination this
  have hdiff_τ : (s' - s) - (h' - h) * vandermondeDiff n R = 0 := by
    have hren : rename τ₀ (s' - s) + rename τ₀ ((h' - h) * vandermondeDiff n R) = 0 := by
      rw [← map_add, hdiff, map_zero]
    have hs_fix : rename τ₀ (s' - s) = s' - s :=
      (mem_symmetricSubalgebra _).mp (Subalgebra.sub_mem _ hs' hs_symm) τ₀
    have hh_fix : rename τ₀ (h' - h) = h' - h :=
      (mem_symmetricSubalgebra _).mp (Subalgebra.sub_mem _ hh' hh_symm) τ₀
    rw [hs_fix, map_mul, hh_fix, rename_vandermondeDiff, hsign_τ₀, Units.smul_def,
      Units.val_neg, Units.val_one, neg_one_zsmul] at hren
    linear_combination hren
  have hs_zero : s' - s = 0 := by
    have h2s : (2 : R) • (s' - s) = 0 := by
      rw [two_smul]
      linear_combination hdiff + hdiff_τ
    have h2s' : C (2 : R) * (s' - s) = 0 := by
      simpa [smul_eq_C_mul] using h2s
    have hmul := congrArg (fun x => C uinv * x) h2s'
    rw [mul_zero, ← mul_assoc, ← map_mul, mul_comm uinv 2, huinv, map_one, one_mul] at hmul
    exact hmul
  have hh_zero : h' - h = 0 := by
    rw [hs_zero, zero_add] at hdiff
    exact (isRegular_vandermondeDiff n R).right.mul_right_eq_zero_iff.mp hdiff
  exact Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (sub_eq_zero.mp hs_zero)) (Subtype.ext (sub_eq_zero.mp hh_zero))

/-- For `2 ≤ n` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, `alternatingPresentationHom n R` is surjective. -/
theorem alternatingPresentationHom_surjective {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    Function.Surjective (alternatingPresentationHom n R) := by
  rintro ⟨p, hp⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨s, h⟩, hp_eq, -⟩ := existsUnique_symmetric_add_mul_vandermondeDiff hn h2 hp
  let A : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := (esymmAlgEquiv (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n)).symm s
  let B : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := (esymmAlgEquiv (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n)).symm h
  refine ⟨rename some A + rename some B * X none, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  have hA : aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) A =
      (s : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) := by
    rw [← esymmAlgHom_apply, ← esymmAlgEquiv_apply (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n),
      AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  have hB : aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) B =
      (h : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) := by
    rw [← esymmAlgHom_apply, ← esymmAlgEquiv_apply (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n),
      AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  simp [hA, hB, hp_eq]

/-- For `2 ≤ n` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, the kernel of `alternatingPresentationHom n R` is the
principal ideal generated by `X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)`. -/
theorem ker_alternatingPresentationHom {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    RingHom.ker (alternatingPresentationHom n R) =
      Ideal.span {X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)} := by
  let rel : MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R := X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · intro P hP
    rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with _ | _
    · rw [Subsingleton.elim P 0]
      exact zero_mem _
    have hopt_rename : ∀ f : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R,
        optionEquivLeft R (Fin n) (rename some f) = Polynomial.C f := fun f => by
      have hcomp :
          (optionEquivLeft R (Fin n)).toAlgHom.comp (rename some) =
            (Polynomial.CAlgHom (R := R) (A := MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) := by
        apply MvPolynomial.algHom_ext
        intro i
        simp [optionEquivLeft_X_some]
      exact AlgHom.congr_fun hcomp f
    let D : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := discriminantPoly n R
    let qpoly : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) := Polynomial.X ^ 2 - Polynomial.C D
    have hq_monic : qpoly.Monic := Polynomial.monic_X_pow_sub_C D (by decide)
    have hq_deg : qpoly.degree = 2 := by
      have hdeg1 : (Polynomial.X ^ 2 : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)).degree = 2 := by
        rw [Polynomial.degree_X_pow]; rfl
      have hdeg2 : (Polynomial.C D : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)).degree <
          (Polynomial.X ^ 2 : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)).degree := by
        rw [hdeg1]
        exact lt_of_le_of_lt Polynomial.degree_C_le (by decide)
      rw [Polynomial.degree_sub_eq_left_of_degree_lt hdeg2, hdeg1]
    let Q := optionEquivLeft R (Fin n) P
    let rem := Q %ₘ qpoly
    let quo := Q /ₘ qpoly
    have hdiv : rem + qpoly * quo = Q := Polynomial.modByMonic_add_div Q qpoly
    have hrem_deg : rem.degree < 2 := hq_deg ▸ Polynomial.degree_modByMonic_lt Q hq_monic
    have hrem_eq : rem =
        Polynomial.C (rem.coeff 0) + Polynomial.C (rem.coeff 1) * Polynomial.X := by
      ext k
      match k with
      | 0 => simp
      | 1 => simp
      | k + 2 =>
        have hlt : rem.degree < (k + 2 : ℕ) :=
          lt_of_lt_of_le hrem_deg (by exact_mod_cast (Nat.le_add_left 2 k))
        rw [Polynomial.coeff_eq_zero_of_degree_lt hlt]
        simp
    let A : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := rem.coeff 0
    let B : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R := rem.coeff 1
    let Q' : MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R := (optionEquivLeft R (Fin n)).symm quo
    have hopt_rel : optionEquivLeft R (Fin n) rel = qpoly := by
      simp [rel, qpoly, D, hopt_rename, optionEquivLeft_X_none]
    have hP_eq : P = (rename some A + rename some B * X none) + rel * Q' := by
      apply (optionEquivLeft R (Fin n)).injective
      rw [map_add, map_add, map_mul, map_mul, hopt_rename A, hopt_rename B,
        optionEquivLeft_X_none, hopt_rel, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
      exact (hrem_eq ▸ hdiv).symm
    have hhom_zero :
        alternatingPresentationHom n R (rename some A + rename some B * X none) = 0 := by
      have hP0 : alternatingPresentationHom n R P = 0 := hP
      rw [hP_eq, map_add, map_mul, alternatingPresentationHom_discriminant_rel, zero_mul,
        add_zero] at hP0
      exact hP0
    have hval_zero :
        aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) A +
          aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) B * vandermondeDiff n R = 0 := by
      have h := congrArg Subtype.val hhom_zero
      simpa using h
    have hAsymm : aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) A ∈
        symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R := by
      rw [← esymmAlgHom_apply]
      exact (esymmAlgHom (Fin n) R n A).2
    have hBsymm : aeval (fun i : Fin n => esymm (Fin n) R ((i : ℕ) + 1)) B ∈
        symmetricSubalgebra (Fin n) R := by
      rw [← esymmAlgHom_apply]
      exact (esymmAlgHom (Fin n) R n B).2
    have huniq := (existsUnique_symmetric_add_mul_vandermondeDiff hn h2
      (zero_mem (permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R))).unique
      (y₁ := (⟨_, hAsymm⟩, ⟨_, hBsymm⟩)) (y₂ := (0, 0))
      (by simpa using hval_zero.symm) (by simp)
    have hA0 : A = 0 := by
      apply (esymmAlgEquiv (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n)).injective
      apply Subtype.ext
      rw [esymmAlgEquiv_apply, esymmAlgHom_apply, map_zero, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero]
      simpa using congrArg (fun x => (x.1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) huniq
    have hB0 : B = 0 := by
      apply (esymmAlgEquiv (Fin n) R (Fintype.card_fin n)).injective
      apply Subtype.ext
      rw [esymmAlgEquiv_apply, esymmAlgHom_apply, map_zero, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero]
      simpa using congrArg (fun x => (x.2 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) huniq
    rw [hP_eq, hA0, hB0, map_zero, zero_mul, add_zero, zero_add]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right Q' _ (Ideal.subset_span rfl)
  · rw [Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
    exact alternatingPresentationHom_discriminant_rel n R

/-- **Presentation of the alternating invariant algebra (`2 ≤ n`, `IsUnit (2 : R)`):**
`R[e₁, …, eₙ, Δ] / (Δ² - Dₙ) ≃ₐ[R] permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R`. -/
noncomputable def alternatingPresentationEquiv {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    (MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R ⧸
        Ideal.span {X none ^ 2 - rename some (discriminantPoly n R)}) ≃ₐ[R]
      permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (ker_alternatingPresentationHom hn R h2).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (alternatingPresentationHom_surjective hn R h2))

@[simp]
theorem alternatingPresentationEquiv_mk {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) (P : MvPolynomial (Option (Fin n)) R) :
    alternatingPresentationEquiv hn R h2 (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ P) =
      alternatingPresentationHom n R P := by
  rw [alternatingPresentationEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk,
    Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_mk]

/-! ### The `n = 1` case -/

/-- For `n = 1`, `alternatingGroup (Fin 1) = ⊥` and its invariant subalgebra is the whole
polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R`. -/
@[simp]
theorem permInvariantSubalgebra_alternatingGroup_one (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 1)) R = ⊤ := by
  have hbot : alternatingGroup (Fin 1) = ⊥ :=
    TauCeti.alternatingGroup_eq_bot_iff.mpr (by simp)
  rw [hbot, permInvariantSubalgebra_bot]

/-! ### Explicit three-variable witness `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` -/

private theorem esymm_three_one (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    esymm (Fin 3) R 1 = X 0 + X 1 + X 2 := by
  have hcard : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 3)).powersetCard 1 =
      {{(0 : Fin 3)}, {(1 : Fin 3)}, {(2 : Fin 3)}} := by decide
  rw [esymm, hcard, Finset.sum_insert (by decide), Finset.sum_insert (by decide),
    Finset.sum_singleton]
  simp [add_assoc]

private theorem esymm_three_two (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    esymm (Fin 3) R 2 = X 0 * X 1 + X 0 * X 2 + X 1 * X 2 := by
  have hcard : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 3)).powersetCard 2 =
      {{(0 : Fin 3), 1}, {(0 : Fin 3), 2}, {(1 : Fin 3), 2}} := by decide
  rw [esymm, hcard, Finset.sum_insert (by decide), Finset.sum_insert (by decide),
    Finset.sum_singleton, Finset.prod_insert (by decide), Finset.prod_singleton,
    Finset.prod_insert (by decide), Finset.prod_singleton, Finset.prod_insert (by decide),
    Finset.prod_singleton, add_assoc]

private theorem esymm_three_three (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    esymm (Fin 3) R 3 = X 0 * X 1 * X 2 := by
  have hcard : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 3)).powersetCard 3 = {{(0 : Fin 3), 1, 2}} := by decide
  rw [esymm, hcard, Finset.sum_singleton, Finset.prod_insert (by decide),
    Finset.prod_insert (by decide), Finset.prod_singleton, mul_assoc]

/-- The polynomial identity `e₁ e₂ - Δ₃ = 2 (x² z + x y² + y z²) + 3 x y z` in three variables. -/
theorem esymm_one_mul_two_sub_vandermondeDiff_three (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    esymm (Fin 3) R 1 * esymm (Fin 3) R 2 - vandermondeDiff 3 R =
      C 2 * (X 0 ^ 2 * X 2 + X 0 * X 1 ^ 2 + X 1 * X 2 ^ 2) +
        C 3 * (X 0 * X 1 * X 2) := by
  have hΔ : vandermondeDiff 3 R = (X 0 - X 1) * (X 0 - X 2) * (X 1 - X 2) := by
    rw [vandermondeDiff, Fin.prod_univ_three]
    have h0 : Finset.Ioi (0 : Fin 3) = {1, 2} := by decide
    have h1 : Finset.Ioi (1 : Fin 3) = {2} := by decide
    have h2 : Finset.Ioi (2 : Fin 3) = ∅ := by decide
    rw [h0, h1, h2, Finset.prod_insert (by decide), Finset.prod_singleton, Finset.prod_singleton,
      Finset.prod_empty, mul_one]
  rw [esymm_three_one, esymm_three_two, hΔ]
  simp only [map_ofNat]
  ring

/-- The explicit three-variable `A₃`-invariant `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` over a commutative ring in which
`2` is a unit. -/
noncomputable def alternatingThreeWitness (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R :=
  C ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R) * (esymm (Fin 3) R 1 * esymm (Fin 3) R 2 - vandermondeDiff 3 R)

/-- `alternatingThreeWitness R h2` lies in
`permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 3)) R`. -/
theorem alternatingThreeWitness_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    alternatingThreeWitness R h2 ∈ permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 3)) R := by
  refine Subalgebra.mul_mem _ (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _) (Subalgebra.sub_mem _ ?_ ?_)
  · exact Subalgebra.mul_mem _
      (symmetricSubalgebra_le_permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 3))
        (esymm_isSymmetric _ _ 1))
      (symmetricSubalgebra_le_permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 3))
        (esymm_isSymmetric _ _ 2))
  · exact vandermondeDiff_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra_alternatingGroup 3 R

/-- Explicit expansion `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2 = x² z + x y² + y z² + (3 / 2) x y z`. -/
theorem alternatingThreeWitness_eq (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    alternatingThreeWitness R h2 =
      X 0 ^ 2 * X 2 + X 0 * X 1 ^ 2 + X 1 * X 2 ^ 2 +
        C (3 * ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R)) * (X 0 * X 1 * X 2) := by
  have hu : ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R) * 2 = 1 := by
    change ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R) * (h2.unit : R) = 1
    exact_mod_cast Units.inv_mul h2.unit
  rw [alternatingThreeWitness, esymm_one_mul_two_sub_vandermondeDiff_three, mul_add, ← mul_assoc,
    ← mul_assoc, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, hu, map_one, one_mul, mul_comm ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R) 3]

end MvPolynomial

/-! ### SAGBI behavior of alternating-group invariants -/

namespace MonomialOrder

open MvPolynomial

/-- For `n = 1`, `{X 0}` is a singleton `m`-SAGBI basis of
`permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 1)) R` for every monomial order `m`. -/
theorem isSAGBIBasis_singleton_X_zero_alternatingGroup_one (m : MonomialOrder (Fin 1))
    (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    m.IsSAGBIBasis {(X (0 : Fin 1) : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R)}
      (permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 1)) R) := by
  rw [permInvariantSubalgebra_alternatingGroup_one]
  have hrange : Set.range (X : Fin 1 → MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R) = {X 0} := by
    ext p
    simp [eq_comm]
  simpa [hrange] using m.isSAGBIBasis_range_X (R := R)

/-- **Nonfinite SAGBI for alternating groups (`n ≥ 3`):** for every `n ≥ 3`, every monomial order
`m`, and every nontrivial commutative semiring `R` without zero divisors (in particular every field
in every characteristic), `permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R` admits no finite
`m`-SAGBI basis. -/
theorem not_exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_alternatingGroup {n : ℕ} (hn : 3 ≤ n)
    (m : MonomialOrder (Fin n)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [NoZeroDivisors R] [Nontrivial R] :
    ¬ ∃ B : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R), B.Finite ∧
        m.IsSAGBIBasis B (permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin n)) R) := by
  rw [m.exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff,
    TauCeti.closure_isSwap_alternatingGroup_eq_iff, Fintype.card_fin]
  omega

private theorem alternatingThreeWitness_eq_monomials (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    alternatingThreeWitness R h2 =
      monomial (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1) (1 : R) +
      monomial (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 1 2) 1 +
      monomial (Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 2 2) 1 +
      monomial (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1)
        (3 * ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R)) := by
  rw [alternatingThreeWitness_eq]
  simp only [X_pow_eq_monomial]
  simp only [X, monomial_mul_monomial, C_mul_monomial, mul_one]

private theorem coeff_alternatingThreeWitness_lead (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    (alternatingThreeWitness R h2).coeff (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1) =
      1 := by
  let d1 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  let d2 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 2
  let d3 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 2
  let d4 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  have hne12 : d2 ≠ d1 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [d1, d2] at this
  have hne13 : d3 ≠ d1 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [d1, d3] at this
  have hne14 : d4 ≠ d1 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [d1, d4] at this
  rw [alternatingThreeWitness_eq_monomials]
  change (monomial d1 (1 : R) + monomial d2 1 + monomial d3 1 +
      monomial d4 (3 * ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R))).coeff d1 = 1
  rw [AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add,
    Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.add_apply,
    coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial]
  simp [hne12, hne13, hne14]

/-- Under lexicographic order `X 0 > X 1 > X 2`, the leading exponent of
`(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` is `x² z = Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1`. -/
theorem lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    MonomialOrder.lex.degree (alternatingThreeWitness R h2) =
      Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1 := by
  let d1 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  let d2 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 2
  let d3 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 2
  let d4 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  let c : R := 3 * ((h2.unit⁻¹ : Rˣ) : R)
  have hf : alternatingThreeWitness R h2 =
      monomial d1 (1 : R) + monomial d2 1 + monomial d3 1 + monomial d4 c :=
    alternatingThreeWitness_eq_monomials R h2
  have hlt2 : d2 ≺[MonomialOrder.lex] d1 := by
    rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
    refine ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), ?_⟩
    simp [d1, d2]
  have hlt3 : d3 ≺[MonomialOrder.lex] d1 := by
    rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
    refine ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), ?_⟩
    simp [d1, d3]
  have hlt4 : d4 ≺[MonomialOrder.lex] d1 := by
    rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
    refine ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), ?_⟩
    simp [d1, d4]
  apply MonomialOrder.lex.toSyn.injective
  refine le_antisymm (MonomialOrder.lex.degree_le_iff.2 fun d hd => ?_) ?_
  · rw [hf] at hd
    have hsub : (monomial d1 (1 : R) + monomial d2 1 + monomial d3 1 + monomial d4 c).support ⊆
        {d1, d2, d3, d4} := by
      refine support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset ?_ (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
      refine support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset ?_ (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
      exact support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp))
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
    have hmem := hsub hd
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hmem
    rcases hmem with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact le_rfl
    · exact hlt2.le
    · exact hlt3.le
    · exact hlt4.le
  · apply MonomialOrder.lex.le_degree
    rw [mem_support_iff, coeff_alternatingThreeWitness_lead]
    exact one_ne_zero

/-- Under lexicographic order `X 0 > X 1 > X 2`, the leading term of `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` is
`X 0 ^ 2 * X 2`. -/
theorem lex_leadingTerm_alternatingThreeWitness (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm (alternatingThreeWitness R h2) = X 0 ^ 2 * X 2 := by
  rw [leadingTerm, leadingCoeff, lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness,
    coeff_alternatingThreeWitness_lead, X_pow_eq_monomial, X, monomial_mul_monomial, one_mul]

/-- The exponent `x² z = (2, 0, 1)` does not belong to the additive submonoid generated by the
leading exponents `x`, `x y`, `x y z`, `x² y` of the four algebra generators `e₁, e₂, e₃, Δ₃`. -/
theorem lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness_notMem_closure :
    (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1) ∉
      AddSubmonoid.closure
        ({Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 1 1} : Set (Fin 3 →₀ ℕ)) := by
  let M : AddSubmonoid (Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :=
    { carrier := {v | v 2 ≤ v 1}
      zero_mem' := by simp
      add_mem' := fun {a b} ha hb => by
        change a 2 ≤ a 1 at ha
        change b 2 ≤ b 1 at hb
        change (a + b) 2 ≤ (a + b) 1
        simp only [Finsupp.add_apply]
        omega }
  have hle : AddSubmonoid.closure
      ({Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1,
        Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1,
        Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1,
        Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 1 1} : Set (Fin 3 →₀ ℕ)) ≤ M := by
    rw [AddSubmonoid.closure_le]
    rintro v (rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl) <;> simp [M]
  intro hmem
  have h := hle hmem
  simp [M] at h

private theorem lex_degree_esymm_three_one (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] :
    MonomialOrder.lex.degree (esymm (Fin 3) R 1) = Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 := by
  let e0 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1
  let e1 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 1 1
  let e2 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 2 1
  have hne1 : e1 ≠ e0 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [e0, e1] at this
  have hne2 : e2 ≠ e0 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [e0, e2] at this
  have he1 : esymm (Fin 3) R 1 = monomial e0 1 + monomial e1 1 + monomial e2 1 := by
    rw [esymm_three_one]; simp only [X, e0, e1, e2]
  rw [he1]
  apply MonomialOrder.lex.toSyn.injective
  refine le_antisymm (MonomialOrder.lex.degree_le_iff.2 fun d hd => ?_) ?_
  · have hsub : (monomial e0 (1 : R) + monomial e1 1 + monomial e2 1).support ⊆ {e0, e1, e2} := by
      refine support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset ?_ (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
      exact support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp))
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
    have hmem := hsub hd
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hmem
    rcases hmem with rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact le_rfl
    · apply le_of_lt
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
      exact ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), by simp [e1]⟩
    · apply le_of_lt
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
      exact ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), by simp [e2]⟩
  · apply MonomialOrder.lex.le_degree
    change e0 ∈ (monomial e0 (1 : R) + monomial e1 1 + monomial e2 1).support
    rw [mem_support_iff, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add,
      Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial]
    simp [hne1, hne2]

private theorem lex_degree_esymm_three_two (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] :
    MonomialOrder.lex.degree (esymm (Fin 3) R 2) =
      Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 := by
  let e01 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1
  let e02 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  let e12 : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1
  have hne1 : e02 ≠ e01 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 1; simp [e01, e02] at this
  have hne2 : e12 ≠ e01 := fun h => by
    have := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) 0; simp [e01, e12] at this
  have he2 : esymm (Fin 3) R 2 = monomial e01 1 + monomial e02 1 + monomial e12 1 := by
    rw [esymm_three_two]; simp only [X, monomial_mul_monomial, one_mul, e01, e02, e12]
  rw [he2]
  apply MonomialOrder.lex.toSyn.injective
  refine le_antisymm (MonomialOrder.lex.degree_le_iff.2 fun d hd => ?_) ?_
  · have hsub : (monomial e01 (1 : R) + monomial e02 1 + monomial e12 1).support ⊆
        {e01, e02, e12} := by
      refine support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset ?_ (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
      exact support_add.trans (Finset.union_subset
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp))
        (support_monomial_subset.trans (by simp)))
    have hmem := hsub hd
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hmem
    rcases hmem with rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact le_rfl
    · apply le_of_lt
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
      refine ⟨1, fun j hj => ?_, by simp [e02]⟩
      have hj0 : j = 0 := Fin.ext (by omega)
      subst hj0
      simp [e02]
    · apply le_of_lt
      rw [MonomialOrder.lex_lt_iff]
      exact ⟨0, fun j hj => absurd hj (Fin.not_lt_zero j), by simp [e12]⟩
  · apply MonomialOrder.lex.le_degree
    change e01 ∈ (monomial e01 (1 : R) + monomial e02 1 + monomial e12 1).support
    rw [mem_support_iff, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add,
      Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial]
    simp [hne1, hne2]

private theorem lex_degree_esymm_three_three (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] :
    MonomialOrder.lex.degree (esymm (Fin 3) R 3) =
      Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1 := by
  classical
  have he3 : esymm (Fin 3) R 3 =
      monomial (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1) 1 := by
    rw [esymm_three_three]; simp only [X, monomial_mul_monomial, one_mul]
  rw [he3, degree_monomial]
  simp

/-- In three variables with lexicographic order `x > y > z` and `IsUnit (2 : R)`, the generating set
`{e₁, e₂, e₃, Δ₃}` of the `A₃`-invariant algebra is not a `lex`-SAGBI basis: the leading exponent
`x² z` of `(e₁ e₂ - Δ₃) / 2` lies outside the monoid generated by their leading exponents. -/
theorem not_isSAGBIBasis_alternatingThreeGenerators (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R]
    (h2 : IsUnit (2 : R)) :
    ¬ MonomialOrder.lex.IsSAGBIBasis
        ({esymm (Fin 3) R 1, esymm (Fin 3) R 2, esymm (Fin 3) R 3, vandermondeDiff 3 R} :
          Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R))
        (permInvariantSubalgebra (alternatingGroup (Fin 3)) R) := by
  have hdeg_e1 := lex_degree_esymm_three_one R
  have hdeg_e2 := lex_degree_esymm_three_two R
  have hdeg_e3 := lex_degree_esymm_three_three R
  have hdeg_Δ : MonomialOrder.lex.degree (vandermondeDiff 3 R) =
      Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 1 1 := by
    rw [lex_degree_vandermondeDiff]
    ext i
    fin_cases i <;> simp
  intro hB
  have hlt_mem : MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm (alternatingThreeWitness R h2) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin R (MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm ''
        ({esymm (Fin 3) R 1, esymm (Fin 3) R 2, esymm (Fin 3) R 3, vandermondeDiff 3 R} :
          Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R))) := by
    rw [hB.adjoin_leadingTerm]
    exact MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm_mem_initialAlgebra
      (alternatingThreeWitness_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra R h2)
  have hsupp_sub : ∀ p ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm ''
        ({esymm (Fin 3) R 1, esymm (Fin 3) R 2, esymm (Fin 3) R 3, vandermondeDiff 3 R} :
          Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R))),
      (p.support : Set (Fin 3 →₀ ℕ)) ⊆ AddSubmonoid.closure
        ({Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1 + Finsupp.single 2 1,
          Finsupp.single 0 2 + Finsupp.single 1 1} : Set (Fin 3 →₀ ℕ)) := by
    intro p hp
    induction hp using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hx
      intro e he
      have he' : e = MonomialOrder.lex.degree b :=
        Finset.mem_singleton.mp (support_monomial_subset (by simpa [leadingTerm] using he))
      rw [he']
      rcases hb with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
      · rw [hdeg_e1]; exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
      · rw [hdeg_e2]; exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
      · rw [hdeg_e3]; exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
      · rw [hdeg_Δ]; exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
    | algebraMap c =>
      intro e he
      have hsup : (C c : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) R).support ⊆ {0} := by
        rw [← monomial_zero']
        exact support_monomial_subset
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp (hsup he)]
      exact zero_mem _
    | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
      refine (Finset.coe_subset.2 support_add).trans ?_
      rw [Finset.coe_union]
      exact Set.union_subset hx hy
    | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
      refine (Finset.coe_subset.2 (support_mul x y)).trans ?_
      rw [Finset.coe_add]
      exact Set.add_subset_iff.2 fun a ha b hb => add_mem (hx ha) (hy hb)
  have hmem_supp : Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 3) 2 + Finsupp.single 2 1 ∈
      (MonomialOrder.lex.leadingTerm (alternatingThreeWitness R h2)).support := by
    rw [lex_leadingTerm_alternatingThreeWitness, mem_support_iff, X_pow_eq_monomial, X,
      monomial_mul_monomial, one_mul, coeff_monomial]
    simp
  exact lex_degree_alternatingThreeWitness_notMem_closure (hsupp_sub _ hlt_mem hmem_supp)

end MonomialOrder
